{"study_accession":"PRJNA1264798","secondary_study_accession":"SRP586206","title":"The Role of FN1 Gene Interference in Neural Differentiation of Human Bone Marrow Mesenchymal Stem Cells","description":"Fibronectin 1 (FN1) gene is responsible for encoding fibronectin, which is involved in cell adhesion, cell migration, extracellular matrix assembly, cell differentiation and proliferation regulation. FN1 has been shown to be involved in osteoblast differentiation and osteoclast differentiation of bone marrow stem cells (BMSCs), but relatively few studies have been conducted on its involvement in neural differentiation. Three FN1 si RNA sequences were designed to explore the FN1 gene (si-417, si-4467 and si-5468). The cells in the neural differentiation culture system of BMSCs in the interference group maintained the spindle-shaped mesenchymal stem cell morphology. The mRNA and protein expression levels of the FN1 gene in the three interference groups were significantly lower than those in the model group (p < 0.05). Alkaline phosphatase staining results showed that the positive rate of the FN1 interference group was also higher than that in the model group. The mRNA and protein expression levels of the four genes related to neural differentiation (MAP2, Tuj1, NSE and DCX) were significantly lower than those in the model group (p < 0.05). In addition, transcriptome sequencing analysis of the control group, model group and interference group showed that Si group and model group has 1047 upregulated genes and 1077 downregulated genes. The differentially expressed genes (DEGs) between the Si group and the model group were mainly significantly enriched in multiple key pathways such as signal transduction, immune response, RNA processing, cell apoptosis and DNA repair. There were 2246 alternative splicing (AS) in the DEGs of model group and Si group, and protein-protein interaction (PPI) analysis of genes with more than a large number of alternative splicing showed that IL-6 was a core gene. This study further investigated the role of FN1 in neural differentiation of BMSCs, which is helpful to reveal the molecular mechanism of stem cell differentiation.","pubmed":"","geo_series":"","n_samples":9,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN48582257","study_accession":"PRJNA1264798","blood_class":"bone_marrow","class_from":"study","title":"Human sample from Homo sapiens","description":"Human sample from Homo sapiens","sex":"not provided","geo_sample":"","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2026-07-22","attributes":[["isolate","homo_sapiens"],["age","miss"],["biomaterial_provider","Zhonghong Botuan Biotechnology Co.,Ltd"],["collection_date","2025-01-27"],["geo_loc_name","China"],["sex","not provided"],["tissue","BMSCs"],["lat_lon","missing"],["lep","c1"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR33618891","experiment_accession":"SRX28847230","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"other","instrument_model":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000","read_count":17397582,"base_count":5170674207,"first_public":"2026-07-22","experiment_title":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000 sequencing: RNA-Seq"}],"labels":[],"single_cell":false},{"sample_accession":"SAMN48582258","study_accession":"PRJNA1264798","blood_class":"bone_marrow","class_from":"study","title":"Human sample from Homo sapiens","description":"Human sample from Homo sapiens","sex":"not provided","geo_sample":"","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2026-07-22","attributes":[["isolate","homo_sapiens"],["age","miss"],["biomaterial_provider","Zhonghong Botuan Biotechnology Co.,Ltd"],["collection_date","2025-01-27"],["geo_loc_name","China"],["sex","not provided"],["tissue","BMSCs"],["lat_lon","missing"],["lep","c2"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR33618890","experiment_accession":"SRX28847231","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"other","instrument_model":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000","read_count":20284653,"base_count":6027542913,"first_public":"2026-07-22","experiment_title":"Illumina NovaSeq 